  "id": "pr-196",
  "instruction": "Standardize how target and argument values are interpreted across glom specifier types (including Match, Switch, Assign, Spec, Call, Invoke, T, and S). Arguments that represent sub-targets or transformation steps must consistently be treated as glom specifications rather than inconsistently treated as literal constants or requiring explicit workarounds.\n\nEnsure that:\n1. Specifier arguments across core operations (e.g., Match default cases, Switch condition and branch specs, Assign values and subspecs) consistently support nested specs, literals (e.g. via Val), target navigators (T), and scope navigators (S).\n2. Spec and recursive spec evaluation correctly resolves targets without crashing on recursion or improperly evaluating sub-expressions.\n3. Match and Switch properly evaluate target specs, match clauses, and fallback/default specs.\n4. Assign handles spec-derived values (including Val and dynamic specs) correctly when assigning back to the target.\n5. T expressions and S scope lookups work seamlessly as subspecs inside other specifier constructs.",
